From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:18:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Clear memory when the OS asks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

*Security* → *Memory protection* → *Clear memory at power-on* was on or
off. Make it a choice of three, the values of security/memory: Always
(1, the default, as on), When the OS asks (2: only when bit 0 of the
TCG MOR variable MemoryOverwriteRequestControl is set, after a reset
while the OS held secrets) and Never (0, as off). A saved on or off
keeps its meaning. The help says what Linux needs: its kernel sets the
request at every boot when RESET_ATTACK_MITIGATION is on, so something
must clear it at a clean shutdown, or the memory is cleared each time.

TEST=Builds for the W541 (mrc and nri); the setup menu of the build
lists the three values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c | 21 +++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
index 02f3f9c402..8ec3b1d04a 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
@@ -474,14 +474,23 @@ static const struct sm_object bootmedia_lock = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
 }, WITH_CALLBACK(update_bootmedia_lock));
 
 /* Read by security_clear_dram_request() (security/memory/memory.c) */
-static const struct sm_object clear_dram_on_boot = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
+static const struct sm_object clear_dram_on_boot = SM_DECLARE_ENUM({
 	.opt_name	= "clear_dram_on_boot",
 	.ui_name	= "Clear memory at power-on",
-	.ui_helptext	= "Clear all the memory at every boot (not when resuming\n"
-			  "from sleep), so that what the previous OS left in it\n"
-			  "cannot be read. About 1.7 s with 32 GB of memory.\n"
-			  "Default: on.",
-	.default_value	= true,
+	.ui_helptext	= "Clear all the memory before the OS starts (not when\n"
+			  "resuming from sleep), so that what the previous OS left in\n"
+			  "it cannot be read: about 1.7 s with 32 GB of memory.\n"
+			  "Always: at every boot. When the OS asks: only after a\n"
+			  "reset while the OS held secrets (TCG MOR: Windows with\n"
+			  "BitLocker; Linux sets the request at every boot and needs\n"
+			  "it cleared at a clean shutdown). Never: not even then.\n"
+			  "Default: Always.",
+	.default_value	= 1,
+	.values		= (const struct sm_enum_value[]) {
+				{ "Always",		1	},
+				{ "When the OS asks",	2	},
+				{ "Never",		0	},
+				SM_ENUM_VALUE_END	},
 });
 
 static const struct sm_object security_flash = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
-- 
